WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
If your prep is SuTab, this video will walk you through exactly how to take it.

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.640
Just follow along step by step. Your SuTab kit includes two bottles of 12

3
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.520
tablets each

4
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:17.290
and a measured container. Start your first dose between 6 and 7 PM the night

5
00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.400
before your procedure.

6
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.800
Open your first bottle of 12 tablets. Fill the provided container with 16

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:24.800
ounces of water

8
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:30.170
up to the fill line. Swallow one tablet every 2 minutes with a sip of water,

9
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:30.560
finishing all

10
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:36.880
12 tablets over about 15 to 20 minutes. Take your time and go at a steady pace.

11
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:43.680
About 1 hour after your last tablet, fill the container again with 16 ounces

12
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:44.480
of water

13
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.860
and drink the entire amount slowly over 30 minutes. Then, about 30 minutes

14
00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:50.640
after finishing

15
00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.300
that container, fill it one more time with 16 ounces of water and drink the

16
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.960
entire amount over 30

17
00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:04.420
minutes. That completes your first dose. 7 hours prior to your procedure,

18
00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:05.360
repeat the exact

19
00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:10.730
same three steps using your second bottle of 12 tablets. One tablet every 2

20
00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:11.760
minutes with water,

21
00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.330
then 16 ounces of water one hour later, then 16 ounces of water 30 minutes

22
00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:17.360
after that.

23
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.000
This part is really important. You must drink all of the prep solution as

24
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.360
directed, even if you're

25
00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:28.200
already passing clear liquid. I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the

26
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.120
entire dose is

27
00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.720
what gives us the clearest view during your procedure. If the prep isn't

28
00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.280
completed as directed,

29
00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:40.080
we may need to reschedule, and neither of us wants that. Between doses, keep

30
00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:40.560
drinking

31
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.840
clear liquids to stay hydrated. It will help you feel better and help the prep

32
00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:45.680
do its job.

33
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:50.320
Do not drink anything at all within 4 hours of your procedure, including

34
00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:50.960
water,

35
00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:56.400
unless it is a small sip to take a medication. Your procedure may be canceled

36
00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.360
or rescheduled if

37
00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.300
this is not followed. If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to

38
00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.200
the bathroom,

39
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:08.060
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

40
00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.320
That's it. You've got this.

41
00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:15.480
Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay hydrated. If you have any

42
00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.720
questions at all,

43
00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:20.000
don't hesitate to call our office. We're here to help.
